Step 2: Recall ROT13 properties

ROT13 is a Caesar cipher with shift of 13. Since there are 26 letters in the alphabet, applying ROT13 twice returns the original text:

    A → N → A

    B → O → B

    etc.

Step 3: Create the decoding command

Use the tr (translate) command to shift letters by 13 positions:
bash

echo "cvpbPGS{Eriref1at_g3kg_Ge4afs0ez@g10af_7n89n9qn}" | tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'

This works because:

    'A-Za-z' matches all uppercase and lowercase letters

    'N-ZA-Mn-za-m' maps:

        A-M → N-Z (first half of uppercase to second half)

        N-Z → A-M (second half of uppercase to first half)

        a-m → n-z (first half of lowercase to second half)

        n-z → a-m (second half of lowercase to first half)

